  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We'd like COBRA to estimate how co-expression among the 220 genes of our targeted immune panel shifts with BMI, adjusting for recruitment site, with both covariates coded numerically in the design table. I'm not sure whether the final export has 180 or 260 samples; it depends on whether the second recruitment wave was merged in."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"estimate how co-expression among the 220 genes of our targeted immune panel shifts with BMI, adjusting for recruitment site, with both covariates coded numerically in the design table\" -- available from COBRA. Not stated in your request: COBRA needs more genes than samples -- checked against your files before any run.\n2. \"the final export has 180 or 260 samples\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set.\n\nSelected path: **COBRA**.\n\nYour question asks for a co-expression network. **COBRA** fits that result.\n\n**COBRA** — Model covariate-associated gene co-expression with COBRA. COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Correcting gene means alone may leave covariance confounding. Covariate-associated components are not TF-to-gene regulatory edges or proof that a covariate causes the expression pattern.\n\nRequired workflow inputs:\n\n- `expression_file`: expression matrix\n- `design_file`: sample covariate design matrix\n\nOutputs:\n\n- `coexpression_network`: Inferred gene-to-gene associations.\n\nAsk for the workflow's controls and defaults if you want to set them.\n\nInput compatibility has not been assessed: your data was not checked against the workflow's required inputs; name your input files to have them checked. This is workflow guidance only; no execution was authorized. No files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
